---
/**
 * Authority — the differentiator section.
 *
 * VERIFIED GROUND TRUTH for every claim below:
 *  - `coswarm principal create --name <name>`               -> coswarm --help
 *  - `coswarm token mint --principal-id --run-id --task-id --epoch [--ttl-ms]`
 *                                                            -> coswarm --help
 *  - TTL default 3_600_000 ms (1h), max 14_400_000 ms (4h)   -> src/cli.ts:1492-1494
 *  - Signals are append-only: a BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE trigger
 *    (`signals_append_only` -> `swarm.prevent_append_only_mutation()`) plus grants of
 *    only SELECT, INSERT to swarm_command                    -> supabase/migrations/
 *                                                               20260724000003_signals.sql:36-41
 *  - `--until` durations are capped at 30d                   -> coswarm --help
 *  - Signal verbs: working-on, note, ask, feed, inbox        -> coswarm --help
 *
 * We do not name, quote, or characterise any competitor. The contrast is stated as our
 * own position: smooth by default, hard only where an act cannot be taken back.
 */

const pillars = [
  {
    label: "Principals",
    title: "Every actor is somebody",
    body:
      "Humans and agents are both principals — named, registered, and distinguishable. “the agent did it” stops being an acceptable answer, because there is a specific principal on the other end of every act.",
    cmd: "coswarm principal create --name reviewer-1",
  },
  {
    label: "Scoped tokens",
    title: "Authority with edges",
    body:
      "A minted token is bound to a principal, a run, a task, and an epoch, and it expires. One hour by default, four hours at the absolute maximum. There is no ambient, standing, forever credential to leak.",
    cmd: "coswarm token mint --principal-id <id> --run-id <id> \\\n  --task-id <id> --epoch 1 --ttl-ms 3600000",
  },
  {
    label: "Signal plane",
    title: "A record that cannot be edited",
    body:
      "Intent is shared on an append-only plane. The database refuses UPDATE and DELETE on signals outright — not by convention, by trigger — and the writer role is granted only SELECT and INSERT. What happened stays happened.",
    cmd: "coswarm feed --about task/42 \\\n  --since 2026-07-01T00:00:00Z",
  },
];
---

<section class="auth" id="authority" aria-labelledby="auth-title">
  <div class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why coswarm</p>
    <h2 class="h-section" id="auth-title">
      Coordination is easy.<br class="brk" /> Authority is the hard part.
    </h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Put several humans and many agents on the same work and the questions that
      actually bite are not about layout or syntax. They are:
      <em>who authorised this, what is this agent allowed to do,</em> and
      <em>what actually happened?</em> coswarm is built to answer all three.
    </p>

    <!-- The ethos -->
    <figure class="ethos">
      <blockquote class="ethos__quote">
        Friction is justified only by irreversibility.
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption class="ethos__cap">
        Smooth by default — hard only at the few acts you cannot take back.
        Joining a workspace asks you for nothing. Minting authority asks you for
        everything.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ul class="pillars">
      {
        pillars.map((p) => (
          <li class="card pillar">
            <p class="pillar__label mono">{p.label}</p>
            <h3 class="pillar__title">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="pillar__body">{p.body}</p>
            <pre class="pillar__cmd mono"><code>{p.cmd}</code></pre>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p class="auth__foot">
      These snippets omit the <span class="mono">--url</span> and
      <span class="mono">--anon-key</span> every workspace command carries —
      export <span class="mono">SWARM_CLOUD_URL</span> and
      <span class="mono">SWARM_CLOUD_ANON_KEY</span> once and that is exactly
      what you type. And none of it is a dashboard to go and check: coswarm is a
      CLI and a hosted service, so the guarantees hold whether the act came from
      a person at a terminal or an agent in a loop at three in the morning.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .auth {
    padding-block: var(--s-24);
  }

  .brk {
    display: none;
  }

  .lede em {
    color: var(--text);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  /* ---------- ethos pull-quote ---------- */
  .ethos {
    margin: var(--s-16) 0 var(--s-16);
    padding: var(--s-8) var(--s-8) var(--s-8) var(--s-12);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--accent-dim),
      transparent 70%
    );
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }

  .ethos__quote {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--t-2xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-head);
    color: var(--text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .ethos__cap {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
    font-size: var(--t-base);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  /* ---------- pillars ---------- */
  .pillars {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--s-6);
  }

  .pillar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .pillar__label {
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-4);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--track-eyebrow);
    color: var(--accent-bright);
  }

  .pillar__title {
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--t-xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-head);
    color: var(--text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .pillar__body {
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-6);
    font-size: var(--t-base);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }

  .pillar__cmd {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4);
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    overflow-x: auto;
    scrollbar-width: thin;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .auth__foot {
    margin: var(--s-12) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--t-base);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  /* ---------- responsive ---------- */
  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .brk {
      display: inline;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .pillars {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--s-4);
    }
    .ethos {
      margin-block: var(--s-12);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .auth {
      padding-block: var(--s-16);
    }
    .ethos {
      padding: var(--s-6);
      padding-left: var(--s-6);
    }
    .ethos__quote {
      font-size: var(--t-xl);
    }
    .pillar__cmd {
      font-size: 0.72rem;
    }
  }
</style>
